Third-party components

The source tree itself depends only on the Go module github.com/BurntSushi/toml
(MIT), whose license ships with the module.

The published container image bundles additional third-party software that is
not part of this repository's source. Those components remain under their own
licenses, and distributing the image means distributing them:

  Jellyfin FFmpeg            GPL-3.0 (or later), depending on build options
                             https://github.com/jellyfin/jellyfin-ffmpeg
  FFmpeg                     LGPL-2.1+ / GPL-2.0+, depending on build options
                             https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html
  Intel media driver (iHD)   MIT
                             https://github.com/intel/media-driver
  Intel oneVPL / Media SDK   MIT
                             https://github.com/intel/libvpl
  Debian base image          various free software licenses
                             https://www.debian.org/legal/licenses/

Corresponding source for the GPL components is available from the projects
linked above. lessarr does not modify them; they are invoked as separate
executables by the container.

No media files, no user configuration and no credentials are ever included in
the image.
